  "supplements": [
    {
      "section": "### 보충 검증 — 새 hard syntax 문항\n\n사후 D3 진단에서 동기를 얻어 새 hard syntax768문항(참·거짓 각384,24wrappers)을 구성·동결한 뒤18개 모델/체크포인트 측정을 완료했다. 학습 완료5개 모델의 정확도는 50.26%–56.12%였고, 원래 D3 괄호 정확도는 88.54%–94.79%였다. 새 문항에서 이 모델들의 yes 응답률은 76.17%–99.22%로, 균형 정확도와 함께 응답 편향을 확인해야 한다. 두 집합은 내용·구조 분포가 달라 점수 차이가 shortcut 사용의 인과적 증거는 아니다. 이 결과는 전체 정확도 gate만으로 재귀 이해를 입증할 수 없음을 강조하며, 새로운 독립 확증 검정이나 원래 주 분석의 변경으로 취급하지 않는다.\n\n![Final models on new hard syntax cases](artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_final_accuracy.svg)\n\n768 balanced rows in24 wrappers; dotted line marks chance50%. These are posthoc-motivated new cases, frozen before inference, outside the110 primary tests.\n\n[그림 데이터](artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_final_accuracy.json)\n\n![Hard syntax cases across five frozen training trajectories](artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_checkpoint_trajectory.svg)\n\nFive separately initialized models; each line reuses one model across checkpoints. No retraining or checkpoint selection. This is not independent replication at each point.\n\n[그림 데이터](artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_checkpoint_trajectory.json)\n\n[18개 전체 측정·신뢰구간·응답 편향·출처](reports/followup-v2/HARD_STRESS_REPORT.md)\n\n",
      "figures": [
        {
          "id": "supplement_hard_final_accuracy",
          "title": "Final models on new hard syntax cases",
          "path": "artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_final_accuracy.svg",
          "png": "artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_final_accuracy.png",
          "receipt": "artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_final_accuracy.json",
          "note": "768 balanced rows in24 wrappers; dotted line marks chance50%. These are posthoc-motivated new cases, frozen before inference, outside the110 primary tests.",
          "show_in_readme": true
        },
        {
          "id": "supplement_hard_checkpoint_trajectory",
          "title": "Hard syntax cases across five frozen training trajectories",
          "path": "artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_checkpoint_trajectory.svg",
          "png": "artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_checkpoint_trajectory.png",
          "receipt": "artifacts/followup-v2/figures/supplement_hard_checkpoint_trajectory.json",
          "note": "Five separately initialized models; each line reuses one model across checkpoints. No retraining or checkpoint selection. This is not independent replication at each point.",
          "show_in_readme": true
        }
      ],
      "limitations": [
        "Post-hoc motivated by D3 local-cue weakness; fresh outcomes do not make it preregistered primary evidence.",
        "Valid strings need suitable closing runs, so their structural distribution differs from the original syntax corpus.",
        "Equal5..8pair length range prevents longer strings being the sole explanation; depth distribution can still differ.",
        "Removing adjacent type mismatches does not remove every finite-state/local cue or prove recursive parsing.",
        "Wrappers were already inspected in D3; only content/outcomes are new.",
        "All18 confidence intervals are descriptive wrapper-cluster bootstrap intervals conditional on fixed models; no global claims are inferred from overlap or individual exploratory p-values.",
        "Balanced true/false pairs make chance accuracy50%; yes preference and true/false accuracy can still be highly asymmetric. Ties count as incorrect.",
        "Different calibration-selected prefix contexts remain for Qwen, Smol and OLMo; matched target content does not mean identical full prompts.",
        "Original D3 and the hard set differ in content and structural distribution. Their difference is not a controlled causal effect or proof of recursive parsing."
      ],
      "report": "reports/followup-v2/HARD_STRESS_REPORT.md"
    }
  ],
